    "image": "https:\/\/www.icrc.org\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/rss\/public\/document\/image\/marie_from_the_drc_is_reconnected_with_her_family_through_the_restoring_family_links_programme.jpg?itok=JdchB14B"
}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{
    "@context": "https:\/\/schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "name": "Frequently asked questions about our work",
    "url": "https:\/\/www.icrc.org\/en\/article\/faq-missing-persons",
    "datePublished": "2026-08-07T08:17:55+02:00",
    "mainEntity": [
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How has the crisis of missing persons evolved, and why is it worsening?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003EThe number of missing persons has risen sharply in recent years. With over 130 conflicts worldwide — double the number recorded in 2009 — the number of people going missing continues to grow. Families are often left in uncertainty for decades, unable to grieve, find closure, or rebuild their lives.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe complexity of family separation and disappearances is also increasing, as migration, disasters, and armed conflicts create new challenges, such as searching the missing across different countries and even continents. Vulnerable individuals, such as unaccompanied minors and detainees, are especially at risk of going missing.\u003C\/p\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is the impact on families of the missing?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003EThe absence of a loved one creates profound emotional, psychological, social, and economic challenges for families. Not knowing the fate of a loved one leaves families in a state of permanent uncertainty, which can lead to unresolved grief and a painful psychological condition known as \u0022ambiguous loss.\u0022\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFamilies must also navigate a range of practical challenges, including legal, social, administrative, economic, and health-related difficulties. The ICRC works to support families and empower them to cope with these challenges while they continue their search for answers.\u003C\/p\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What role do families of the missing play beyond being directly affected?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003EFamilies of the missing are not just victims; they are advocates for answers, justice, and peace. Their resilience and determination play a crucial role in keeping the issue visible and can help foster reconciliation and peacebuilding in affected communities. Families have the right to know the fate of their loved ones, and their advocacy is vital to driving political action and ensuring accountability.\u003C\/p\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Can disappearances and family separations be prevented?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003EYes, preventing people from going missing is possible through adherence to international humanitarian law (IHL) and international human rights law (IHRL). Key preventive measures include:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e3dc0738011d1c84f511d625e694d6b10\u0022\u003EPreserving family unity and preventing separation.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ef39e68413ede8615d53219417cb2a756\u0022\u003EEnsuring the dignified management of the dead.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e06956b944b406b0cea60b312f2226645\u0022\u003EKeeping records of vulnerable individuals, such as unaccompanied minors and detainees, as early as possible to prevent disappearances.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e7f5a97a29729bdda6ec5684c37f6ffed\u0022\u003EEstablishing mechanisms like National Information Bureaux to collect and share information about protected persons, such as prisoners of war, during international armed conflicts.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ul\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What are States’ responsibilities in addressing the issue of missing persons?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003EStates and parties to armed conflict bear the primary responsibility for preventing people from going missing, accounting for those who do, and addressing the needs of families. Under international humanitarian law (IHL) and international human rights law (IHRL), they are obligated to:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ea954f9be171546a6e7ddde6bdac2d56b\u0022\u003EPrevent family separations and maintain family unity.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e93f01d2b18f462d53a8fd4ea222108e1\u0022\u003EProvide information about the fate and whereabouts of missing persons to their families.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e60fb5a97adba971c545974a9b5659535\u0022\u003EEnsure the proper management of the dead, including identification and burial.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e3d25989fa96642979cfe41d0c30bc1fa\u0022\u003EStrengthen medico-legal systems and establish mechanisms like National Information Bureaux to collect and share information about missing persons.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESustained political commitment is essential, even during conflict or decades later, to create an environment that prioritizes the suffering of families and brings answers, justice, and dignity.\u003C\/p\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is the ICRC’s role in reconnecting families and addressing the issue of missing persons?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003EFor over 150 years, the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) has worked to prevent family separations, reconnect families, and search for missing persons. The Central Tracing Agency (CTA), established in 1870 and enshrined in the Geneva Conventions, is at the heart of these efforts.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe ICRC’s work includes:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e664c6cb7871b9010ccdc128491f025d9\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EHelping families stay in touch:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Acting quickly during emergencies to prevent the loss of contact and disappearances through tools like free phone or video calls, Red Cross messages, and other communication methods.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e4ddf049b6bcf8a9b7812893649b8cf2f\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EAccounting for and searching for missing people:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Keeping track of the whereabouts of vulnerable individuals and conducting tailored searches for missing persons.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ea3e085dde72400f9ba7576c839742747\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESupporting families:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Empowering families to cope with the psychological, social, legal, and economic challenges caused by the absence of loved ones, and to advocate for their needs\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e0fe8523591a006df50a7ac4fa6450435\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EInfluencing and advocating:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Working with family associations, civil society, states and other actors to prevent and address family separation and disappearances, sharing best practices, and providing expert advice to help them fulfill their obligations.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ul\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How does the ICRC search for missing persons?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003ESearching for missing persons is a complex process that requires tailored approaches for each situation. The ICRC uses a variety of methods, including:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ed0c26675f7a67fabbf58741da34dd8fd\u0022\u003EFieldwork on individual cases.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e7a8b633df8f3cdbc043db4fff2560932\u0022\u003EData analysis and, identity matching, and new technologies, such as advanced algorithms to connect and analyse information across platforms and borders.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e2505126cf61b449b32acb06b17bd524c\u0022\u003EDialogue with authorities to ensure they fulfil their obligations to prevent disappearances, search for missing persons, and address families’ needs.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022eb6ed7be19878907da6e75ed6484e4dde\u0022\u003EAccessing hard-to-reach areas.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e8591d575840acd01eabfef7aa33d0026\u0022\u003EForensic science, including the identification of the deceased.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ul\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How does the ICRC support families of the missing?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003ET\u003Ca\u003Ehe ICRC and the Family Links Network provide comprehensive support to families, such as:\u003C\/a\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e4bb0f2eb5ec52af0dc97c59382b6f984\u0022\u003ECommunication tools such as phone or video calls and Red Cross messages to help families stay in touch with loved ones.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ec7ea6c7b3c72a34c48e8173bea7fa48a\u0022\u003EOnline tools like\u0026nbsp;\u003Cem\u003ETrace the Face\u003C\/em\u003E to assist in searches.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ed93a7b530638099aba9e605d59bdb890\u0022\u003Epsychological, legal, social, and economic support to help families cope with ambiguous loss.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ec26ab673b266b07b620858b6003c1521\u0022\u003EEmpowerment initiatives to help families advocate for their missing loved ones and collaborate with others for mutual support.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ul\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Why is addressing the issue of missing persons essential for peacebuilding and reconciliation?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cp\u003EUnresolved cases of missing persons perpetuate trauma, deepen grievances, and hinder community healing long after violence has ended.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e9fd6d7f80dc7e28442a7dbce7cc856c2\u0022\u003EThe absence of answers and acknowledgment fuels resentment, affecting family histories and identities across generations. Without meaningful responses, wounds remain open, and reconciliation becomes impossible.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ea37cb2081ee32b5ff6749cbcdd68caa0\u0022\u003EUnaddressed cases perpetuate instability and hinder peacebuilding. Families report that the unresolved issue of missing persons is often exploited to fuel divisions and prolong conflicts.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e048a1002b0c21ed0c2c1733d05113de9\u0022\u003EConversely, addressing this issue can counteract manipulation, foster trust, and build confidence among conflicting parties. Including the issue of missing persons in political negotiations can advance conflict prevention, support reconciliation, and sustain long-term peace processes.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ul\u003E"
            }
        },
        {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What steps can be taken to support families of the missing and promote peacebuilding?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e992dbaffc8d961703a9697a6f0db9118\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPrioritize families’ needs:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Centre all efforts on the emotional, legal, economic, and administrative needs of families, ensuring support for both the search process and their well-being.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022ed0ca63ce6efd86ca881ed609d31f2d10\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EEngage in conflict-sensitive approaches:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Acknowledge how the issue of the missing can be exploited to sustain divisions. A focus on humanitarian needs fosters peacebuilding and reconciliation.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e6fac7da3bf367c184baf9ca58928bd64\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EFoster connection across divides:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Bringing families of the missing together, including those from opposing sides, helps prevent isolation, encourages shared understanding, and empowers families as peacebuilders.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e049412d473db28db00ed635e44387182\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESupport family-led peacebuilding:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Families should be encouraged to engage in joint activities that promote dialogue, solidarity, and reconciliation at the community level, shaping initiatives based on their own needs and wishes.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli data-list-item-id=\u0022e7e57deb3578815a494a688d05b4f51e2\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPromote political commitment:\u003C\/strong\u003E\u0026nbsp;Governments should recognize families of the missing as agents in their own right, not just victims, and include the issue of the missing in political negotiations. Authorities must ensure families’ right to know the fate of their loved ones and address their needs without discrimination.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ul\u003E"
            }
        }
    ]
}</script>
